   574→  - _ulid: 01KF96T3VVQ8CTXQYQ4XNMTQ1W
   575→    type: question
   576→    content: >-
   577→      Shadow branch PR workflow clarification: When work only updates shadow branch (.kspec/)
   578→      metadata - task state, inbox items, notes - should PRs still be created? Ralph instructions
   579→      say 'create PR after commit' but this seems intended for code changes on feature branches.
   580→      Shadow changes track the work; code changes are the work output. Current behavior: skip PR
   581→      when working tree is clean. Need clarification on whether meta manifest changes should follow
   582→      different review process than code changes.
   583→    created_at: '2026-01-18T18:45:21.404Z'
   584→    author: '@claude'
   585→    resolved: false
   586→    resolution: null
   587→  - _ulid: 01KF96T6E67ZB7FVJ8JEDBKTYS
   588→    type: success
   589→    content: >-
   590→      Iteration workflow patterns: (1) Verification-only iterations produce no commits - efficient,
   591→      avoids code churn, skipping PR is correct when working tree clean. (2) Implementation vs
   592→      verification task distinction - verification tasks are quick wins for automation loops,
   593→      implementation tasks need focused sessions. (3) Iteration findings show shadow branch is
   594→      source of truth for task state (git status on main shows clean after adding inbox items),
   595→      session context can be stale. Pattern: prioritize verification in loops, save implementation
   596→      for context-rich sessions.
   597→    created_at: '2026-01-18T18:45:24.039Z'
   598→    author: '@claude'
   599→    resolved: false
   600→    resolution: null
   601→  - _ulid: 01KF96TKTHJ8DNBGCTR8ACQ7DN
   602→    type: success
   603→    content: >-
   604→      PR review momentum: When reviewing own PRs from previous iterations, fix trivial issues
   605→      directly (like invalid ULIDs) rather than leaving comments. Merge when checks pass unless
   606→      changes are substantial. This keeps momentum going in automation loops.
   607→    created_at: '2026-01-18T18:45:37.746Z'
   608→    author: '@claude'
   609→    resolved: false
